Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 01:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tinkatink line Cormorian Dragon-Slayer Clan palette
 (Dreamstone Ruination starters)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the canonical normal palettes for the Tinkatink evolution line with
the Cormorian Dragon-Slayer Clan identity: soft lavender body, white pigtails
and head-tuft hair, copper/bronze hammer with warm wood handle. This is the
third and final starter palette set for the project (Frigibax and Teddiursa
already shipped).

Per the project bible, all three starter options are permanently 'shiny' from
selection (the form players see is always the Cormorian palette), so these
changes go in normal.pal/overworld_normal.pal rather than shiny.pal. The
canonical shiny palettes are not modified — they remain accessible only via
mechanisms players cannot reach in normal play.

Per-species design notes (palette-only approach, no PNG modifications):

Tinkatink:
- Body: soft cool lavender (canonical pink family -> lavender)
- Head-tuft: pure white with cool-grey shadow (canonical pink-cream tuft -> white)
- Hammer head: copper-bronze metal (canonical purple metal -> copper)
- Hammer-stick handle: warm dark wood
- Compromise: back.png canonical-artist mismatch causes the front-view cheek-mark
  accent to collapse into body shadow color. The cheek shape is preserved through
  silhouette outline but the contrasting magenta accent is lost. Per the user-
  approved palette-only-approach decision, this compromise is accepted rather
  than addressed via per-pixel PNG modification.

Tinkatuff:
- Body: soft cool lavender (canonical pink body -> lavender)
- Pigtails: pure white (canonical pink-cream pigtails -> white)
- Hammer: copper-bronze metal mass with dark wood handle
- Compromise: cheek-mark accent collapsed to body-shadow color (same constraint
  as Tinkatink). Accepted per palette-only approach.

Tinkaton:
- Body: soft cool lavender (canonical magenta-pink body -> lavender)
- Pigtails: pure white with off-white midtones (canonical pink fluff -> white)
- Hammer: copper-bronze metal head with warm dark wood handle
- Crimson cloth wrap not added (would require per-pixel surgical edits; deferred
  per palette-only decision)

Color identity (all values multiples of 8 for GBA-safe runtime fidelity):
  Body main:        (176, 152, 208) - soft lavender (the workhorse body color)
  Body highlight:   (208, 184, 224) - light lavender for face/upper body shines
  Body shadow:      (128, 104, 160) - lavender shadow
  Body deep:        ( 88,  72, 120) - deep lavender (lower body shadows)
  Body outline:     ( 56,  40,  88) - deep lavender outline
  Hair main:        (232, 232, 240) - off-white pigtail/tuft main
  Hair highlight:   (248, 248, 248) - pure white shine
  Hair shadow:      (176, 176, 200) - cool grey hair shadow
  Hammer main:      (168, 104,  56) - copper-bronze workhorse
  Hammer highlight: (240, 192, 120) - bright copper highlight
  Hammer light:     (208, 144,  72) - copper midtone
  Hammer shadow:    (112,  64,  40) - deep copper shadow
  Hammer deep:      ( 72,  40,  24) - deepest copper
  Wood main:        ( 96,  64,  40) - warm dark wood handle
  Wood shadow:      ( 56,  32,  16) - deeper wood shadow

Approach:
- Per-index sprite analysis (Section 10.1 of DREAMSTONE_HANDOFF.md methodology):
  isolation views of every palette index, semantic mapping to body parts
- Front.png and back.png have different embedded palettes (Dracovish quirk noted
  in Section 4.3 of the handoff doc) — analyzed both independently, chose palette
  values that work reasonably for both views' index assignments
- Overworld.png has its own 16-color palette with different index meanings than
  the battle sprite — analyzed independently per Section 4.4
- Stale compiled artifacts deleted (normal.gbapal, normal.gbapal.lz,
  overworld_normal.gbapal, overworld_normal.gbapal.lz) — build's '%.gbapal: %.pal'
  rule will regenerate them
- No PNG byte-level modifications; this is a pure .pal file patch

Files modified per species:
  graphics/pokemon/tinkatink/{normal.pal, overworld_normal.pal}
  graphics/pokemon/tinkatuff/{normal.pal, overworld_normal.pal}
  graphics/pokemon/tinkaton/{normal.pal, overworld_normal.pal}

Verification:
1. Apply patch in source tree
2. Stale compiled gbapal binaries already removed; make rule '%.gbapal: %.pal'
   will rebuild them on next compile
3. Compile (make modern)
4. Players selecting the Tinkatink starter line will see the Cormorian Dragon-
   Slayer Clan identity throughout battle (front/back) and overworld (follower)
   sprites
